Titanic Survival Prediction – EDA Summary Report

Objective
The objective of this project was to analyze the Titanic dataset, preprocess the data, and predict passenger survival using machine learning models.

Data Preprocessing
Loaded the dataset and identified numerical and categorical columns.
Handled missing values in Age, Cabin, and Embarked.
Removed duplicate records and treated outliers using the IQR method.
Encoded categorical variables and applied StandardScaler to numerical features.
Exploratory Data Analysis
Analyzed the Survived column to understand the distribution of survivors and non-survivors.
Explored the relationship between Passenger Class, Gender, and Survival.
Visualized the data using histograms, line charts, scatter plots, and a correlation heatmap.
Model Building

Built and evaluated Logistic Regression and Decision Tree models using an 80:20 train-test split.

Conclusion

The analysis showed that gender, passenger class, age, and fare influenced passenger survival. Both models performed well, and the model with the higher accuracy was selected as the better predictor.
